<https://example.org/wikigraph/snapshot/wikipedia/33194455/1374937776> <https://example.org/wikigraph/text> "Mobile operating system for iPad tablets Operating system iPadOS Screenshot of iPadOS 27 Developer Apple Written in C , C++ , Objective-C , Swift , assembly language OS family Unix-like , based on Darwin ( BSD ), iOS , macOS Working state Current Source model Closed with open-source components Initial release September 24, 2019 ; 6 years ago ( 2019-09-24 ) Latest release 27.0 (September 14, 2026 ; 4 days ago ( 2026-09-14 ) ) [±] Latest preview 27.2 beta (September 16, 2026 ; 2 days ago ( 2026-09-16 ) ) [±] Marketing target Tablet computers Available in 40 languages Update method Over-the-air , iTunes , Finder Supported platforms ARMv9-A ( 17.4 –present) ARMv8-A ( 13.0 –present) Kernel type Hybrid ( XNU ) Default user interface Cocoa Touch ( multi-touch , GUI ) License Proprietary software except for open-source components Preceded by iOS Official website apple.com/os/ipados Articles in the series iPadOS version history iPadOS is a proprietary mobile operating system created and developed by Apple for its iPad line of tablet computers . It was given a name distinct from iOS , the operating system used by Apple's iPhones , to reflect the diverging features of the two product lines, such as multitasking. The operating system was introduced as iPadOS 13 , reflecting its status as the successor to iOS 12 for the iPad, and first released to the public on September 24, 2019. Major versions of iPadOS are released annually; the current stable version, iPadOS 27 , was released to the public on September 14, 2026 ( 2026-09-14 ) . ^ \"iPadOS\" . Apple Inc. Archived from the original on December 15, 2019 . Retrieved June 3, 2019 . ^ Clover, Juli (September 14, 2026). \"Apple Releases iOS 27 and iPadOS 27 With Siri AI and Liquid Glass Update\" . MacRumors . Retrieved September 14, 2026 . ^ \"Apple Releases First iOS 27.2 Beta\" . MacRumors . September 16, 2026 . Retrieved September 16, 2026 . ^ \"Apple – iPad Pro – Specs\" . Apple Inc. Archived from the original on January 4, 2019 . Retrieved January 4, 2019 . ^ \"Apple – iPad mini 4 – Specs\" . Apple Inc. Archived from the original on October 24, 2015 . Retrieved October 24, 2015 . ^ \"Apple – iPad Air 2 – Technical Specifications\" . Apple Inc. Archived from the original on October 26, 2015 . Retrieved October 24, 2015 . ^ \"Apple – iPhone XS – Technical Specifications\" . Apple Inc. Archived from the original on January 4, 2019 . Retrieved January 4, 2019 . ^ Jariwala, Abhishek (June 4, 2019). \"Everything Announced at the Apple WWDC 2019 Conference: iPadOS, Mac Pro, iOS 13, MacOS Catalina and More\" . TrueTech . Archived from the original on November 26, 2020." .
