<https://example.org/wikigraph/snapshot/wikipedia/562879/1373070928> <https://example.org/wikigraph/text> "Compiler for Haskell programming language Glasgow Haskell Compiler Original author Kevin Hammond Developers Simon Marlow , Simon Peyton Jones , The Glasgow Haskell Team Release December 1992 ; 33 years ago ( 1992-12 ) Stable release 9.14.1 / 19 December 2025 ; 8 months ago ( 19 December 2025 ) Written in Haskell , C Operating system Linux , macOS 10.7 and later, Windows Vista and later, FreeBSD Platform x86 (linux only), x86-64 , AArch64 Available in English Type Compiler License BSD 3-clause (new) Website www .haskell .org /ghc Repository gitlab .haskell .org /ghc /ghc .git The Glasgow Haskell Compiler ( GHC ) is a native or machine code compiler for the functional programming language Haskell . It provides a cross-platform software environment for writing and testing Haskell code and supports many extensions, libraries , and optimisations that streamline the process of generating and executing code. GHC is the most commonly used Haskell compiler. It is free and open-source software released under a BSD license . ^ Cite error: The named reference contribs was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference history was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ \"Download – The Glasgow Haskell Compiler\" . Haskell.org . Archived from the original on 28 February 2021 . Retrieved 11 February 2021 . ^ a b \"Download Version 9.12.2 (released 14th Mar 2025)\" . GHC Team. ^ \"Deprecation of 32-bit Darwin and Windows platforms\" . GHC Team. ^ \"The Glorious Glasgow Haskell Compilation System User's Guide\" . Haskell.org . Retrieved 27 July 2014 . ^ \"2017 state of Haskell survey results\" . taylor.fausak.me . 15 November 2017 . Retrieved 11 December 2017 ." .
