<https://example.org/wikigraph/snapshot/wikipedia/57174306/1375583354> <https://example.org/wikigraph/text> "Largest and most influential technology companies in the world The largest corporations by market capitalization in 2026, with the \"Big Five\" tech companies in green Big Tech , also known as the tech giants or tech titans , are the largest and most powerful technology companies in the world. It most commonly refers to the five dominant companies in the U.S. technology industry— Microsoft , Apple , Alphabet ( Google ), Amazon , and Meta ( Facebook )—which are also some of the largest companies in the world by market capitalization , making up about a quarter of the S&P 500 . Other large technology companies, such as Netflix , Nvidia , Tesla , and SpaceX , are sometimes included but usually referred to separately. The term Big Tech is similar to terms for other powerful industries, such as Big Media , Big Oil , Big Pharma , and Big Tobacco . Careers in Big Tech, particularly in technical fields such as software engineering and product management , are considered highly competitive. ^ Attributed to multiple references: Soni, Aditya (October 27, 2025). \"Big Tech to report earnings under specter of AI bubble\" . Reuters . Archived from the original on October 27, 2025 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Nicol-Schwarz, Kai (February 6, 2026). \"Amazon Leads Big Tech's $1 Trillion Wipeout as AI Bubble Fears Ignite Sell-Off\" . CNBC . Archived from the original on February 6, 2026 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Romm, Tony (January 17, 2020). \"Companies Burned by Big Tech Plead for Congress to Regulate Apple, Amazon, Facebook, and Google\" . The Washington Post . ISSN 0190-8286 . Archived from the original on January 17, 2020 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Radsch, Courtney (November 27, 2023). \"The Real Story of the OpenAI Debacle is the Tyranny of Big Tech\" . The Guardian . ISSN 0261-3077 . Archived from the original on November 27, 2023 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Beard, Alison (January 1, 2022). \"Can Big Tech Be Disrupted?\" . Harvard Business Review . Archived from the original on December 15, 2021 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . \"Breaking Up with Big Tech: A Human Rights–Based Argument for Tackling Big Tech's Market Power\" . Amnesty International . August 28, 2025. Archived from the original on August 28, 2025 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . ^ Attributed to multiple references: Satariano, Adam; Mozur, Paul (March 13, 2026). \"U.S. Tech Giants Flocked to the Persian Gulf. Now They Are Targets\" . The New York Times . ISSN 0362-4331 . Archived from the original on March 14, 2026 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Kaye, Danielle (October 29, 2025). \"Tech Giants Are Spending Big on AI in Rush to Dominate the Boom\" . BBC News . Archived from the original on October 29, 2025 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Arroyo, Carmen; Barbuscia, Davide (March 12, 2026). \"How Big Tech's AI Ambitions Are Fueling a Borrowing Boom\" . Bloomberg News . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Hill, Kashmir (February 7, 2019). \"I Cut the 'Big Five' Tech Giants From My Life. It Was Hell\" . Gizmodo . Archived from the original on February 7, 2019 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Woollaston-Webber, Victoria (November 29, 2016). \"This one chart reveals how many European firms have been bought by Apple, Amazon and Alphabet\" . Wired . Archived from the original on February 23, 2025 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . ^ Attributed to multiple references: Rana, Preetika; Dotan, Tom (October 30, 2023). \"Tech Titans Rebound From Tough Times as AI Fuels Optimism\" . The Wall Street Journal . ISSN 0099-9660 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Ovide, Shira (July 29, 2021). \"Big Tech Has Outgrown This Planet\" . The New York Times . ISSN 0362-4331 . Archived from the original on July 29, 2021 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . \"How to tame the tech titans\" . The Economist . January 18, 2018. Archived from the original on April 20, 2018 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Tapp, Tom (April 22, 2022). \"New EU Regulations Will Force Meta, Amazon, Apple And Other Tech Titans To Police Platforms Aggressively Or Face Stiff Fines\" . Deadline Hollywood . Archived from the original on April 23, 2022 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . McNamara, Deborah; Weihl, Bill (March 10, 2025). \"Tech Giants Are complicit in an Anti-Climate Agenda. Employees Should Be Speaking Up\" . Fast Company . Archived from the original on March 16, 2025 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . ^ Khanal, Shaleen; Zhang, Hongzhou; Taeihagh, Araz (April 4, 2025). \"Why and How Is the Power of Big Tech Increasing in the Policy Process? The Case of Generative AI\" . Policy and Society . 44 (1): 52– 69. doi : 10.1093/polsoc/puae012 . ISSN 1449-4035 . ^ Saura García, Carlos (2024). \"Datafeudalism: The Domination of Modern Societies by Big Tech Companies\" . Philosophy & Technology . 37 (3) 90. doi : 10.1007/s13347-024-00777-1 . hdl : 10234/208358 . ^ Attributed to multiple references: Herrman, John (November 13, 2019). \"We're Stuck With the Tech Giants. But They're Stuck With Each Other\" . The New York Times . ISSN 0362-4331 . Archived from the original on November 14, 2019 . Retrieved April 22, 2020 . Birch, Kean; Bronson, Kelly (February 14, 2022). \"Big Tech\" . Science as Culture . 31 (1): 1– 14. doi : 10.1080/09505431.2022.2036118 . Taplin, Jonathan (July 14, 2017). \"Can the Tech Giants Be Stopped?\" . The Wall Street Journal . ISSN 0099-9660 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . \"Big Tech\" . Brave . March 13, 2023. Archived from the original on March 26, 2023 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Wittenstein, Jeran; Vlastelica, Ryan (October 29, 2025). \"AI Spending Is What Matters Most in Alphabet, Microsoft Earnings\" . Bloomberg News . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . DeFrancesco, Dan; Barr, Alistair; Stewart, Ashley; Kim, Eugene; Langley, Hugh; Dixit, Pranav (October 27, 2025). \"Big Tech Earnings Are Almost Here. These Are the Biggest Storylines Worth Watching\" . Business Insider . Archived from the original on October 27, 2025 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . Bozovic, Novak (December 1, 2025). \"What is Big Tech and who does it include?\" . ExpressVPN . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . AP Stylebook [@APStylebook] (May 27, 2020). \"The term Big Tech refers to the technology companies that dominated global commerce throughout the 2010s. Generally this includes Google, Apple, Microsoft, Facebook and Amazon. But it shouldn't be understood to exclude other large U.S. tech companies. #APStyleChat (1/3)\" ( Tweet ). Archived from the original on May 28, 2020 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 – via Twitter . ^ Vlastelica, Ryan (April 17, 2025). \"Netflix Defies Big Tech Slump as Wall Street Seeks Tariff Haven\" . Bloomberg News . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . ^ Randewich, Noel (January 21, 2018). \"Where Netflix Goes, Big Tech May Follow\" . Reuters . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . ^ Newman, Daniel (August 11, 2025). \"Opinion: Alphabet, Meta, Amazon and Microsoft Share This One Thing—And It'll Keep the Stocks Fired Up\" . MarketWatch . Archived from the original on August 11, 2025 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . ^ Metz, Cade; Weise, Karen; Isaac, Mike (January 29, 2024). \"Nvidia's Big Tech Rivals Put Their Own A.I. Chips on the Table\" . The New York Times . ISSN 0362-4331 . Archived from the original on January 29, 2024 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . ^ Jaisinghani, Sagarika; Ponthus; MacDonogh, Isolde (December 17, 2025). \"Tesla's Rally to Record High Is Leaving Big Tech Peers Behind\" . Bloomberg News . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . ^ Liedtke, Michael (April 21, 2025). \"Tesla Kicks Off Earnings Season for Big Tech's 'Magnificent 7' Amid Huge Market Cap Drops Spurred by 'Massive Uncertainty and Chaos' from White House\" . Fortune . Archived from the original on April 21, 2025 . Retrieved March 14, 2026 . ^ Alexandra S. Levine (February 26, 2021). \"Is Twitter angling to become Big Tech?\" . Politico . Retrieved August 8, 2021 . ^ Dang, Sheila; Balu, Nivedita (July 29, 2021). \"From Facebook to Twitter, Big Tech sees social commerce driving sales growth\" . Reuters . Archived from the original on July 29, 2021 . Retrieved August 8, 2021 . ^ Oremus, Will (November 17, 2017). \"Big Tobacco. Big Pharma. Big Tech?\" . Slate . Archived from the original on November 29, 2018 . Retrieved November 22, 2021 . ^ \"How to get into big tech companies (FAANG+) in 7 steps\" . IGotAnOffer . Retrieved April 7, 2026 ." .
